      "content_html": "<img src=\"https://img.hobbyfarms.com/can-chickens-eat-corn-scaled.jpeg\" style=\"width:100%;max-height:300px;object-fit:cover;\" />\n<img src=\"https://img.hobbyfarms.com/can-chickens-eat-corn-scaled.jpeg\" style=\"width:100%;max-height:300px;object-fit:cover;\" />\n<img src=\"https://img.hobbyfarms.com/can-chickens-eat-corn-scaled.jpeg\" style=\"width:100%;max-height:300px;object-fit:cover;\" />\n<img src=\"https://img.hobbyfarms.com/can-chickens-eat-corn-scaled.jpeg\" style=\"width:100%;max-height:300px;object-fit:cover;\" />\n<img src=\"https://img.hobbyfarms.com/can-chickens-eat-corn-scaled.jpeg\" style=\"width:100%;max-height:300px;object-fit:cover;\" />\n<p>Can chickens eat corn? Yes. Corn is a popular treat for backyard chickens and can provide extra energy, especially during cold weather. But like any treat, corn should be fed in moderation. Here&#8217;s what to know about the different types of corn chickens can eat, how much to offer and which forms to avoid. Key [&#8230;]</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.hobbyfarms.com/can-chickens-eat-corn/\">Can Chickens Eat Corn?</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.hobbyfarms.com\">Hobby Farms</a>.</p>",
